## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience with governance, cross-repo data sharing, and policy-as-code in real fintech environments.

## Key Concepts
- cost-governance patterns
- terraform_remote_state data source
- policy as code (OPA)
- CI gating of plans

## Code Example
```javascript
# Minimal budget fetch (pseudo-terraform)
data "terraform_remote_state" "budget" {
  backend = "s3"
  config = {
    bucket = "gov-budgets";
    key    = "costs/${var.env}.tfstate";
    region = "us-east-1";
  }
}
locals {
  monthly_budget = data.terraform_remote_state.budget.outputs["monthly_budget"]
}
```
```javascript
# Minimal OPA policy sketch
package terraform.costs
deny[msg] {
  planned_cost := input.planned_cost
  budget := input.monthly_budget
  planned_cost > budget
  msg = sprintf("Budget exceeded: %v > %v", planned_cost, budget)
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you scale this to handle multi-region budgets?
- How would you add tests to verify gating behavior in CI?

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical understanding of per-env isolation using workspaces, ensuring policy via gates, not just code.

## Key Concepts
- Terraform workspaces
- GCS backend prefixing
- Wrapper modules for consistent labeling
- GitHub Actions plan gating with json + jq

## Code Example
```javascript
// wrappers/env_wrap/main.tf (skeleton)
variable 'environment' {}
variable 'cost_center' {}
```
```javascript
// backend.tf (skeleton)
terraform {
  backend 'gcs' {
    bucket = tf_state_bucket
    prefix = terraform/${terraform_workspace}
  }
}
```
```javascript
// gate.sh (skeleton)
terraform init
terraform plan -out=tfplan
PLAN_JSON=$(terraform show -json tfplan)
# simple policy: if changes exist beyond tag updates, fail
```

